          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "A theme park charges $18 for a child ticket.",
              "marks": []
            },
            {
              "type": "break"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The total cost of two adult tickets and three child tickets is $110.",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p74-q14-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Find the value of an adult ticket.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\$28$.",
          "worked": "Let $x$ be the price of an adult ticket in dollars.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\n2x + 3(18) &= 110 \\\\\n2x + 54 &= 110 \\\\\n2x &= 56 \\\\\nx &= 28\n\\end{align*}$$\n\nAn adult ticket costs $\\$28$.\n\nCheck: $2(28)+3(18)=110$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 48
      },
      {
        "id": "p74-q14-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Find the cost for a party of 6 adults and 13 children to visit the theme park.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\$402$.",
          "worked": "Using the adult-ticket price from part a, the total cost $C$ in dollars is\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\nC &= 6(28)+13(18) \\\\\nC &= 168+234 \\\\\nC &= 402\n\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe party pays $\\$402$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 28
      }
    ]
  },
